 ],
 "literal": "In the morning having risen, a swift chariot having prepared, / bright-ornamented women to embrace, who went / the lord of the fertile town, he delayed until night greatly, saying, / the bewildered little boy's mother, / is tormented, alas, in this status being born indeed.",
 "translation": "Rising early in the morning, he readied his swift chariot and went to embrace women wearing bright ornaments. Because the lord of this fertile town has delayed so long into the night, the mother of his bewildered little boy is in deep torment. Alas, how painful it is to be born into this status of a wife!",
 "modern": "காலையில் எழுந்து வேகமான தேரை ஆயத்தம் செய்து, பிரகாசமான ஆபரணங்களை அணிந்த பரத்தையரைத் தழுவச் சென்ற வளமான ஊரின் தலைவன், இரவு வரை மிகவும் தாமதித்துவிட்டான் என்று எண்ணி, கலங்கும் தன் சிறு மகனின் தாயான தலைவி வருந்துகிறாள். ஐயோ, இந்த இல்லறத் தலைவி என்ற நிலையில் பிறப்பது மிகவும் துன்பம் தருவதாகும்.",
 "explanation": "This poem is set in the Marutam (agricultural) landscape, where the theme is infidelity and the wife's sulking. The speaker is the heroine's friend (தோழி), who is expressing her deep sympathy and frustration on behalf of the heroine. The hero has left early in the morning in his swift chariot to visit courtesans, and has delayed his return until late at night. The heroine, who is the mother of his young, innocent son, waits in anguish and bewilderment. The friend laments the painful fate of women born into the status of a wife, who must endure such neglect and betrayal. The key words are 'எல்லினன்' (he delayed until night) and 'தெறுவது' (it is tormenting), highlighting the emotional pain caused by the hero's unfaithfulness.",
